From: HarmonyOS PC adaptation <adapt@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Makefile: configurable toolchain, portable staged install

The upstream Makefile hard-codes both the toolchain and the installation
mechanics:

    CC = gcc
    CFLAGS = -O3 -Wall
    STRIP = -s
    DEST=

and its install rule runs

    install -m 755 -o root -g root $(STRIP) uucpsend $(DEST)/usr/lib/news/bin

so

  * the compiler and its options can only be steered by a bare command-line
    override, and the unconditional `-s` cannot be turned off for a debug
    build;
  * there is no staging prefix -- `$(DEST)` is only ever a *prefix*, and the
    rule writes straight to it;
  * a non-root builder cannot install at all, because `-o root -g root` is
    passed unconditionally (the obvious workaround, `OWNER=` on the command
    line, yields `install -o -g ...`, which consumes the next argument);
  * `make` with no argument is a hard error: the only rule defined is
    `uucpsend:`, there is no `all:` target.

Changes:

  * Add an `all:` target (`all: uucpsend`) so the conventional default goal
    works, and make `install` depend on the program.  The existing
    `uucpsend: $(OBJS)` rule is kept verbatim: it carries no recipe, so GNU
    make's built-in `%: %.o` rule performs the link, and the `$(OBJS)`
    prerequisite list is what puts both `uucpsend.o` AND `log.o` on the link
    line.  (Replacing that rule instead of adding to it silently links only
    `uucpsend.o`, which fails with undefined references to `openlogfile`,
    `closelogfile` and `filelog` -- observed on device.)
  * CC/CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS and the new BINDIR/CONFDIR/MANDIR/DESTDIR use
    the conventional `?=` form, so the environment supplied by a build
    system (a Conan buildenv script, Debian's dpkg build helpers, ...) takes
    effect while the historical values stay as defaults.  A variable passed
    on the make command line still wins over both the environment and `?=`.
  * STRIP defaults to `-s` only when DEBUG is unset, so debug and
    relwithdebinfo builds keep their symbols.
  * The install rule is rewritten to be POSIX-portable and staging-friendly:
    directories are created with `mkdir -p` instead of `install -d`, file
    modes are set with `-m` only, and no implicit ownership change is
    attempted.  Ownership is a packaging concern and belongs to whoever
    stages the tree, not to `make install`; this is also what makes the rule
    usable by an unprivileged builder.  BINDIR/CONFDIR/MANDIR keep their
    upstream default locations, so a bare `make DESTDIR=/stage install`
    reproduces the historical layout (`/usr/lib/news/bin`, `/etc/news`,
    `/usr/man/man8|man5`) exactly, while still allowing a recipe to redirect
    the configuration file away from /etc.
  * SHELL is pinned to /bin/sh rather than /bin/bash: the only shell code is
    the POSIX for/if loop in the install rule, and /bin/bash is not present
    on every POSIX target (OpenHarmony/HarmonyOS ships /bin/sh only).

The vestigial `DEST=` variable is dropped: it was a non-standard spelling of
a staging prefix that DESTDIR now covers, and nothing outside these install
rules referenced it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]
Signed-off-by: HarmonyOS PC adaptation <adapt@example.invalid>
---
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -16,28 +16,37 @@
 
 #  Makefile for uucpsend
 
-CC = gcc
-CFLAGS = -O3 -Wall
-DEST=
+SHELL = /bin/sh
+CC ?= gcc
+CFLAGS ?= -O3 -Wall
+CPPFLAGS ?=
+LDFLAGS ?=
+DESTDIR ?=
+BINDIR ?= /usr/lib/news/bin
+CONFDIR ?= /etc/news
+MANDIR ?= /usr/man
 MAN=man
 NEWS=news
 OBJS=uucpsend.o log.o
-STRIP=-s
+STRIP=$(if $(DEBUG),,-s)
+
+all: uucpsend
 
 uucpsend: $(OBJS)
 
 clean:
 	rm -f $(OBJS) uucpsend
 
-install:
-	for d in $(DEST)/usr/lib/news/bin $(DEST)/etc/news $(DEST)/usr/man/man{5,8}; \
+install: uucpsend
+	for d in $(DESTDIR)$(BINDIR) $(DESTDIR)$(CONFDIR) $(DESTDIR)$(MANDIR)/man5 \
+	         $(DESTDIR)$(MANDIR)/man8; \
 	do \
-	  if [ ! -d $$d ]; then install -m 755 -o root -g root -d $$d ; fi; \
+	  if [ ! -d $$d ]; then mkdir -p $$d ; fi; \
 	done
-	install -m 755 -o root -g root $(STRIP) uucpsend $(DEST)/usr/lib/news/bin
-	install -m 644 -o $(NEWS) -g $(NEWS) uucpsend.ctl $(DEST)/etc/news
-	install -m 644 -o $(MAN) -g $(MAN) uucpsend.8 $(DEST)/usr/man/man8
-	install -m 644 -o $(MAN) -g $(MAN) uucpsend.ctl.5 $(DEST)/usr/man/man5
+	install -m 755 $(STRIP) uucpsend $(DESTDIR)$(BINDIR)/uucpsend
+	install -m 644 uucpsend.ctl $(DESTDIR)$(CONFDIR)/uucpsend.ctl
+	install -m 644 uucpsend.8 $(DESTDIR)$(MANDIR)/man8/uucpsend.8
+	install -m 644 uucpsend.ctl.5 $(DESTDIR)$(MANDIR)/man5/uucpsend.ctl.5
 
 
 log.o: log.c log.h
